WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:07.038
Across generation, networks and critical energy infrastructure, field work
depends on controlled instructions and the engineering

00:07.038 --> 00:08.293
evidence behind them.

00:08.293 --> 00:16.653
Before a planned task is approved, reviewers need to know which standard
governs, which revision applies and what the inspection

00:16.653 --> 00:17.489
evidence supports.

00:17.489 --> 00:22.505
Cortessa is designed to help authorised teams investigate that bounded
document estate.

00:22.505 --> 00:30.030
It makes source routes and documentary questions visible without becoming an
operational system or taking the approval decision.

00:31.030 --> 00:37.242
A planned-outage or asset-maintenance pack can connect group engineering
standards, site instructions, inspection records, asset

00:37.242 --> 00:39.726
policies, approved deviations and external references.

00:39.726 --> 00:45.110
Those documents may be maintained by different teams and revised on different
schedules.

00:45.110 --> 00:52.564
The review problem is establishing whether the governing source is present and
current, whether terminology and applicability align,

00:52.564 --> 00:59.190
and whether every important statement can be traced back to evidence the
authorised reviewer can inspect.

01:00.190 --> 01:07.475
Cortessa's target energy-site deployment gives each authorised engineer a
dedicated, self-sufficient box inside the site boundary.

01:07.475 --> 01:15.215
Local standards, work packs, inspection evidence, ingestion, index, on-device
model and source viewer remain on that box.

01:15.215 --> 01:19.768
Audit and Ask run locally against the engineer's approved corpus.

01:19.768 --> 01:23.410
Author remains in development and requires further testing.

01:23.410 --> 01:31.150
The engineer controls the working context and remains responsible for
applicability, asset judgement and every approved revision.

01:32.150 --> 01:39.963
Engineer boxes are designed to connect through engineering,
operations-assurance and asset-integrity departmental nodes to an on-site

01:39.963 --> 01:40.451
hub.

01:40.451 --> 01:47.776
The complete exchange stays inside the air-gapped site, with selected
cross-department sharing only where authorised.

01:47.776 --> 01:53.147
This is the target site architecture, not a deployed production-network claim.

01:53.147 --> 02:00.472
The offline revision contract and application foundations exist; authenticated
transport, key operations, scheduling, backup, recovery,

02:00.472 --> 02:03.890
site assurance and rollout remain deployment work.

02:03.890 --> 02:09.750
Cortessa is not connected to supervisory control, protection, scheduling or
live operations.

02:10.750 --> 02:14.167
Audit is the centre of the Cortessa workflow.

02:14.167 --> 02:21.001
It works across the selected work pack rather than waiting for one question at
a time.

02:21.001 --> 02:27.409
It can surface stale or superseded references, missing documentary links,
terminology differences and effectivity questions.

02:27.409 --> 02:34.670
Each candidate enters engineering review; it is not automatically evidence of
equipment failure, non-compliance or unsafe operation.

02:35.670 --> 02:40.435
Every audit result leads back to the passages that created it.

02:40.435 --> 02:47.365
Engineering and assurance specialists can open the source, inspect surrounding
wording and check revision and applicability.

02:47.365 --> 02:52.563
If evidence is absent, Cortessa can refuse rather than fill the gap.

02:52.563 --> 03:00.359
Authorised specialists decide whether the issue is genuine, material, already
controlled or outside scope, then record the outcome

03:00.359 --> 03:02.092
through the existing process.

03:02.092 --> 03:05.990
Verified shows provenance; it does not establish asset condition.

03:06.990 --> 03:12.894
Engineering and operational decisions depend on asset context, site rules and
authorised judgement.

03:12.894 --> 03:20.159
The responsible people decide which document governs, whether a discrepancy
matters and whether work may proceed.

03:20.159 --> 03:23.792
Cortessa makes the evidence route and uncertainty visible.

03:23.792 --> 03:32.421
It does not approve a work pack, determine asset health, authorise an outage
or replace engineering, operations, asset-integrity or

03:32.421 --> 03:33.329
safety authority.

03:33.329 --> 03:37.870
Formal decisions remain in the operator's controlled processes and systems.

03:38.870 --> 03:46.214
An engineer-approved revision can carry signed identity, content hash, parent
lineage and approved audit context through its

03:46.214 --> 03:49.670
departmental node and, where authorised, the on-site hub.

03:49.670 --> 03:56.582
Conflicts and missing ancestry remain visible; the hub does not choose an
operational or engineering answer.

03:56.582 --> 04:02.198
Receipt does not certify a document or make it current or searchable
automatically.

04:02.198 --> 04:05.222
The receiving engineer governs import and use.

04:05.222 --> 04:11.270
The local Ledger supports inspection but does not replace work-control, asset
or approval records.

04:12.270 --> 04:16.326
Compare matched tasks against the existing review baseline.

04:16.326 --> 04:24.946
Measure time to identify and open the governing instruction, reviewer effort,
cited candidate findings, reviewer usefulness and

04:24.946 --> 04:29.002
duplicate rates, appropriate refusals and sampled source-path reproducibility.

04:29.002 --> 04:33.059
Include difficult revisions, excluded evidence and ambiguous terminology.

04:33.059 --> 04:36.101
Record setup, ingestion and corpus-curation effort.

04:36.101 --> 04:47.763
The evaluation should show where Cortessa helps, where it fails and what must
change before any decision to extend the document set or

04:47.763 --> 04:48.270
workflow.

04:49.270 --> 04:51.626
Bring one controlled work pack.

04:51.626 --> 05:01.048
Agree the asset scope, reviewers, baseline and evidence standard, then test
the route from local evidence work to governed departmental

05:01.048 --> 05:01.990
revision exchange.

05:01.990 --> 05:09.528
Cortessa claims no energy deployment, completed site rollout, outage
reduction, availability gain, saving, compliance or safety

05:09.528 --> 05:09.999
outcome.

05:09.999 --> 05:15.181
The architecture must be demonstrated and assured in a representative
environment.

05:15.181 --> 05:18.950
Start a conversation about a scoped energy evaluation.
